## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of persistent data structures and O(1) updates without copying.

## Key Concepts
- Persistence via structural sharing
- Node-based linked representation
- Versioning by top pointer
- Space-time trade-offs and edge cases

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node { constructor(val, prev){ this.val = val; this.prev = prev; } }
class PersistentStack {
  constructor() { this.versions = [null]; } // version 0: empty
  push(version, val) { const top = this.versions[version]; const node = new Node(val, top); this.versions.push(node); return this.versions.length - 1; }
  pop(version) { const top = this.versions[version]; if (!top) return version; this.versions.push(top.prev); return this.versions.length - 1; }
  top(version) { const t = this.versions[version]; return t ? t.val : null; }
  isEmpty(version) { return this.versions[version] == null; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you manage memory for old versions (garbage collection)?
- How would you expose the API to external callers (version IDs, immutability guarantees)?
- Could you adapt this to a persistent queue or other structures with similar patterns?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine a hashmap with a priority structure to track a dynamic mode under duplicates, while keeping updates O(log n) on average. It also checks handling of stale entries and edge cases (removals of non-existent values).

## Key Concepts
- Hash map for value-to-count to enable O(1) updates
- Max-heap keyed by (count, -value) to prioritize higher counts and break ties toward smaller values
- Lazy deletion of stale heap entries to keep updates efficient
- Edge cases: removing non-existent values, empty multiset

## Code Example
```javascript
class ModeMultiset {
  constructor() {
    this.cnt = new Map();
    this.heap = []; // max-heap of [count, -value]
  }
  _heapPush(item) { /* standard binary-heap insert with comparator by count desc, value asc */ }
  _heapPop() { /* standard binary-heap extract-max */ }
  addValue(x) {
    const c = (this.cnt.get(x) || 0) + 1;
    this.cnt.set(x, c);
    this._heapPush([c, -x]);
  }
  removeValue(x) {
    const c = this.cnt.get(x);
    if (!c) return;
    const nc = c - 1;
    if (nc > 0) this.cnt.set(x, nc);
    else this.cnt.delete(x);
    if (nc > 0) this._heapPush([nc, -x]);
  }
  getMode() {
    while (this.heap.length) {
      const [c, neg] = this.heap[0];
      const v = -neg;
      if ((this.cnt.get(v) || 0) === c) return v;
      this._heapPop();
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

